.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# The name without a slash covers a symbolic link as well: a link is not
# a directory, and it has no business in the history either.
node_modules
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
coverage/
*.log
*.backup
.DS_Store
backups/
tmp/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Scratch tooling installed on the server (playwright-core, ws)
tools/
# The tools of the panel bridge are the scripts the operator runs on the panel
# host. The one that creates a key stays out of the history, because it names
# the account of the owner of the panel. The ones that import and update an egg
# are part of the history, because they change the eggs the products run on.
!panel-bridge/tools/
panel-bridge/tools/*
!panel-bridge/tools/blipmade-import-egg.php
!panel-bridge/tools/blipmade-update-egg.php
# The icon font of Font Awesome Pro is licensed and the repository is
# public, so the files are placed on the machine by
# scripts/download-fontawesome-pro.py and are not in the history.
# See docs/TYPOGRAPHY.md.
web/public/fontawesome/
# The before and after screenshots of the interface. They are a review
# artefact, not source, and they would make the history heavy.
screenshots/
# The secrets of the machine: the address of the Discord channel of the
# alarms and anything else that only the owner of the machine may read. The
# files are written by scripts/set-discord-webhook.sh and never travel with
# the history of the repository.
secrets/

# The screenshots of the live site, taken for the report of a round.
.shots/
# The results of the browser tests.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/

# The cache of the Python of the generator of the manifest.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
